From 1020b7b423a0f091d5e11b425b5ef46c39f16777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:35:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usage: the Sessions tab's token totals count the cache, as
 the Overview's do (#2591)

n1majne3 reports the usage totals ignoring the cache reads the same page
shows beside them. The Overview's totals have counted the cache on request
since #2378 (magpie.usageWithCache); the Sessions tab counted tokens in and
out alone wherever they showed: the tokens tile, a session's row in both
lists (the Usage page's and the Sessions page's, sessSpent), the projects
and models bars and pickers (sessSums, spent), the day chart's bars,
tooltips and calendar, and the top sessions. A reader who asked for the
cache on the Overview saw two different totals for the same period.

The tab now reads usageTokens everywhere, so the one pick decides for both
pages. Its tokens tile carries the same label pop-up and says the cache's
count in its line; a pick made there refreshes the tab it is on, not the
Overview. The chart's day and week buckets carry the cache's counts now
that their value reads them, and the top sessions, ranked without the
cache, are ranked again by the count the reader sees. The default stays
without the cache, as #2378 left it; the per-session median and p90 stay
counted in and out (Stats.Overview ranks them), and the Requests tab's
totals always counted every token (allTokens).

Run at 89521b03 + this: sessions-cache-tokens.test.cjs (new; Chromium and
WebKit, en and zh, APIs faked) fails on the base with "AssertionError: the
tile's tokens: '57.0K' !== '168K'" and passes with the change;
sessions-overview, usage-overview-fold, api-key-usage and
sessions-usage-open pass with it (120 tests, both engines, en and zh).
Broken by hand, each red at its own assertion: the pick's callback pinned
back to renderUsage() (the tab doesn't follow the pick), the top list's
re-ranking left out ("ranked by the count shown"), and the day buckets
without their cache counts ("the day's tokens count the cache").

